rradius installed from a package
================================

The package installs the program, the RADIUS dictionaries and the documentation, and creates
the system user "rradius" and the directories /var/lib/rradius (data) and /var/log/rradius.
It does not create a configuration and does not start the service: the service starts only
once /etc/rradius/rradius.toml exists.

First start
-----------

  1. Print a starting configuration; it has random cluster and client secrets:

       rradiusd config init > /etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  2. Edit it. The service can write only below /var/lib/rradius and /var/log/rradius, and
     a relative path in the file is taken from the directory of the file, so set:

       [cluster] data_dir = "/var/lib/rradius"
       [radius.accounting_spool] dir  (if used) below /var/lib/rradius
       [radius.accounting_log] file   (if used) below /var/log/rradius

     "dictionary" already points at /usr/share/rradius/dictionary. Add the [lua] script and
     your clients, and keep the file readable by the "rradius" user only:

       chown root:rradius /etc/rradius/rradius.toml && chmod 640 /etc/rradius/rradius.toml

  3. Check, then start:

       rradiusd check
       systemctl enable --now rradius

     The package does not enable the service by itself.

Splitting the configuration
---------------------------

The directory /etc/rradius/conf.d is created empty. The configuration that "config init"
writes has include = ["conf.d/*.toml"], so every .toml file you put there is read with
rradius.toml, as if its text followed it. A file there begins with a table, for example
[[radius.clients]], and cannot set what rradius.toml or another file sets. A package upgrade
leaves rradius.toml, which you changed, and conf.d alone. "rradiusd config show" prints
the settings of all the files together. Keep the files readable by the "rradius" user only and
writable by root only: an included file can change who may log in, and the server warns about
one that its group or others can write.

The default configuration path is fixed when the program is built; "rradiusd --version"
shows it on the second line.

Documentation: /usr/share/doc/rradius/manual/README.md (start there) and usage.md.
The examples of the manual are in /usr/share/doc/rradius/examples.
